{"author":{"id":"7be502fc1252faa17034e20337c97f83224cb75681f6f2358da33e4e8d7e55b6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794790605,"nonce":"5v6ZJwonapvWD7bk0DPsWoLmtuI=","title":"Static file cache serves stale content after replacing a file with one of the same size","message":"Hello Zentinel team,\n\nthank you for Zentinel. This is a low-priority observation about the static file cache.\n\nObserved (tag 26.11_2, commit ea8ccf0), with a `static-files` route whose root is a symlink:\n\n- After switching the symlink to a directory with a file of the same size but different content, the old content is still served, also after 20 seconds. The ETag and Last-Modified headers are old as well.\n- After SIGHUP the new content is served immediately.\n- With a file of a different size the new content is served immediately.\n\nCause as far as we can tell: a cached entry is used when it is younger than DEFAULT_MAX_AGE_SECS (3600, crates/proxy/src/static_files/cache.rs:13 and is_fresh at cache.rs:186-190) and its size equals the current file size (crates/proxy/src/static_files/mod.rs:330-337). The metadata of the file is read on every request (mod.rs:262-269), and the ETag is built from size and mtime (mod.rs:277-278, 389-394), but the cache check compares only the size. A related effect: two files with the same size and the same mtime (for example from an archive extracted with a fixed mtime) get the same ETag.\n\nRequest: invalidate a cache entry when the modification time (and ideally the inode or file identity) differs from the cached one, not only the size. That would make atomic release switches via symlink work without a reload.\n\nHappy to test a fix. Thank you.","files":null}]}